  "id": "wh5x0zw",
  "title": "Chapter 13: Cell Structure",
  "order": 62,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ug2k94y",
      "content": "The cell is the basic structural and functional unit of life. All living organisms are made up of cells. Cells perform all the essential functions necessary for survival such as metabolism, growth, reproduction and response to stimuli."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
