    {
      "id": "m9n841x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Discovery of the Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Robert Hooke first discovered cells in cork in 1665, while Leeuwenhoek observed living cells in 1674.",
        "Cell Theory was formulated by Schleiden and Schwann, and expanded by Rudolf Virchow with 'Omnis cellula-e-cellula'.",
        "Prokaryotic cells lack a membrane-bound nucleus, whereas Eukaryotic cells contain a well-defined nucleus and membrane-bound organelles.",
        "Mitochondria generate ATP (powerhouse of the cell), while Ribosomes are responsible for protein synthesis.",
        "Plant cells possess cell walls, plastids, and large vacuoles, which are typically absent or smaller in animal cells."
      ],
      "id": "ycef1fa"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r39ivkk",
      "content": "• Robert Hooke discovered the cell in 1665 while observing cork under a microscope."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bjr3xes",
      "content": "• He described the small compartments as 'cells'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "guzu1hx",
      "content": "• Anton van Leeuwenhoek later observed living cells using a microscope."
    },
    {
      "id": "1sdfj0l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Cell Theory"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1ik38k6",
      "content": "• All living organisms are composed of cells."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a7exq09",
      "content": "• The cell is the basic unit of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "noa26md",
      "content": "• All cells arise from pre-existing cells."
    },
    {
