    {
      "id": "higlm6a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Difference Between Plant Cell and Animal Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mature mammalian Red Blood Cells (RBCs) lack a nucleus, with exception to Camel and Llama.",
        "Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semi-autonomous organelles containing their own circular DNA and 70S ribosomes.",
        "Lysosomes are frequently referred to as 'suicidal bags' due to their hydrolytic digestive enzymes.",
        "The plant cell wall is composed of cellulose, whereas the fungal cell wall is composed of chitin."
      ],
      "id": "9kdn0h4"
    },
